course: dictionary
lesson: 13943
title: Lethargy: a heavy, tired feeling
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Lethargy is a noun. It means a heavy feeling of having no energy and not wanting to do anything. «After three nights of bad sleep, Sam felt lethargy all day.» Sam did not want to run, play or even talk much, so lethargy must mean that heavy, tired feeling.
explain: Look for clues around the word. Words like heavy, slow, sleepy, tired or «no energy» often sit close to lethargy. Check your meaning by swapping it into the sentence: «Sam felt a heavy tiredness all day» still makes sense, so you know you have the right meaning.
explain: Lethargy can last for a long time and can be a sign that something is wrong. Doctors and scientists look at it as a clue about our health, along with things like sleep, food and water.
fact: Lethargy means a heavy feeling of having no energy and not wanting to do anything.
fact: Lethargy is an uncountable noun, so we do not usually say "a lethargy" or "two lethargies".
fact: Lethargy can be a sign of illness, lack of sleep, poor food or not enough water.
fact: In stories, «a hot afternoon of lethargy» tells the reader that people are very tired and slow.
fact: The adjective is lethargic, as in «She felt lethargic after the flu.»
exercise: «After three nights of bad sleep, Sam felt lethargy all day.» What does lethargy mean? | A loud noise in the classroom | A sharp pain in the leg | *A heavy feeling of having no energy | A bright, happy feeling of running fast
exercise: «A hot afternoon of lethargy made the whole village slow and quiet.» What does lethargy tell the reader? | The people were racing to the river | The people were singing loudly | The people had just won a prize | *The people were very tired and slow
exercise: Mia has had lethargy for a week and cannot get out of bed. Which could be a reason for lethargy? | Winning a race | Eating too many apples in the park | *Illness or not enough sleep | Being given a new bike
test: Which of these can cause lethargy? | A cold swim in the sea | A loud song at school | A big hug from a friend | *Not enough water
test: Lethargy is best described as: | A sharp, stinging pain | *A heavy, tired feeling with no energy | A type of bright light | A fast, excited feeling
exam: Which sentence shows lethargy? | *«He lay on the sofa all afternoon, too heavy and tired to move.» | «The bell rang and the children cheered.» | «She jumped up, grabbed her bag and ran out.»
